// An enameler of the craftsmen's quarter at Bibracte, setting red glass into
// bronze harness bosses.
=== start
She has a bronze boss in a clamp and a little crucible on the coals, and she's setting red glass into the hollows of a pattern with a needle, one drop at a time.

"For somebody's horse," she says, without looking up. "A great man's horse. They all want red. It's always red." She blows on it. "Mind the crucible."
* "Whose horse?" -> whose
* "Goodbye." -> END

=== whose
"Somebody up the hill." She tips her head at the inner bank. "They all ride now. Every boy with a father on the council wants a harness that shines." She sets another drop. "Good for business. War's good for business. Everybody says so."
* "Goodbye." -> END
